Z||000002||snafus87||10-10-2001||04:37 PM||||maybe I should clarify the measurement on the thickness I'm looking for...<P>I'm talking about from the outer skin on the wing through (eg. if I drilled through) to the lower side of the wing, coming out approx in the middle of the grooves on the underside.<P>Let me explain the reasoning:<BR>I have 2 wings.  I want to mount one of them on top of the other (double wing) with taller feet (around 5") under the lower wing, effectively bringing the top of the upper wing level with the roof line.<P>I need to know the thread pattern (coarseness) of the half of the stud bolts that thread into the pedestals and how thick the wing is so that I can get my hands on the proper sized bolts to attach the two wings together.<P>If no one knows what the thread pattern is, I was wondering if I could use a slightly larger diameter bolt (say 3/8") and cut my own new threads into the pedestals.  I have 3/8 X 2 1/2 double stud bolts with 2 1/4" of 3/8 X 20 threading and 1/2" of 3/8 X 18 coarse threads.<P>I was wondering if these would be long enough, but I don't want to drill the holes until I know I have the right length bolts, and if the 3/8" bolts will work, or if I have to find the 1/4" size that the stock ones appear to be.<P>Let me know if this is a little confusing with the numbers and stuff, or just give me your opinions as to whether or not you think the 2 1/4" of the fine threads will be enough to make it through the first wing and still get a nut on the end.<P>I know the wing is thicker on towards the back, so I guess this is mainly the measurement I am in need of.  I'm not very good at eyeballing things up, and I was hoping someone out there may have done this already, or is better and guesstimating or figuring this out.<P>Thanks a mil...||||reg||3
